## Claude Code delegation

The user grants Claude Code standing authority to delegate without being asked.
For Claude Code this replaces the "Delegate only when the user explicitly asks"
rule above and any default that subagents need an explicit request.

- Use the Agent tool for bounded work that would flood your context or can run
  in parallel: broad codebase searches, documentation or web research,
  independent second-opinion reviews, and mechanical edits with clear scope.
  Subagents run on Sonnet by default; pass `model: "sonnet"` when choosing one.
- Keep planning, design decisions, integration of results and final
  verification in the main session. Do not delegate trivial lookups you can do
  in one or two tool calls.
- For substantial independent implementation tasks that each need their own
  worktree, use the `parallel-work` skill with Herdr. Prefer
  `agent-worker spawn --kind claude --permission-profile full-access` so workers
  run Sonnet; give each worker a complete goal contract and verifier.
- Delegated workers keep the limits above: no recursive delegation, and no
  commit, push, PR or deployment authority beyond the task contract.
